ived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":0,"created_at":"2025-11-26T22:31:21Z","updated_at":"2025-11-27T11:20:12Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nReproducible in current master and 4.5.1\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.6.dev (db7479cfc) - Windows 10 (build 19045) - Single-window, 1 monitor - Vulkan (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce RTX 3080 (NVIDIA; 32.0.15.8157) - AMD Ryzen 9 5950X 16-Core Processor (32 threads) - 63.91 GiB memory\n\n### Issue description\n\nWhen word wrap is enabled in the script editor and extreme cases with many wrapped lines are encountered, both the accuracy of the visible area rectangle in the minimap as well as its drag detection will fail.\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/eac64f53-ad40-4795-bc40-2fd470435060\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Open MRP.\n2. Enable minimap in Editor Settings if disabled.\n3. Disable word wrap if enabled (Alt+Z) and try dragging minimap to note its accuracy.\n4. Enable word wrap, and try dragging.\n5. Try dragging scroll bar to note its inaccuracy.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[minimap-wrap-problem.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/23780704/minimap-wrap-problem.zip)","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113215/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113215/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null}